# No em dash / en dash

Never use Unicode em dash (U+2014) or en dash (U+2013) in Sociva code, comments, UI copy, docs, SQL, notifications, DB user-facing text, or Codemagic YAML.

Always use a plain ASCII hyphen-minus (U+002D): `-`

Examples:
- Bad: `Home-cooked dum biryani` + em dash + ` layered the slow way`
- Good: `Home-cooked dum biryani - layered the slow way`

When editing or generating text, if you see U+2014 or U+2013, replace with `-`. Prefer spaced hyphen (` - `) over glued hyphens for clause breaks.

This avoids an "AI-generated" look in the product.
